# ZigML Optimizer Library

> A high-performance, research-grade deep learning optimization library written in Zig,
> targeting modern GPU architectures — with first-class support for the **NVIDIA B200 Blackwell** GPU.

---

## Overview

This library provides a self-contained, zero-dependency implementation of state-of-the-art
gradient-based optimizers and training utilities. It combines multiple cutting-edge
research ideas — Sophia, SOAP/K-FAC, MARS variance reduction, spectral normalization,
mixed-precision training, and Bayesian hyperparameter search — into a single, unified
framework built entirely in Zig, with manual memory management and no external ML library
dependencies.

The project is part of a larger codebase and depends on three sibling modules:

```
../core/types.zig
../core/tensor.zig
../core/memory.zig
```

