## Core Components

### Tensor

The fundamental data structure. All tensors store data as a flat `[]f32` slice with a
separate `Shape` struct holding the dimension list.

```zig
// Create a 3×4 zero-initialized tensor
var t = try Tensor.zeros(allocator, &[_]usize{ 3, 4 });
defer t.deinit();

// Fill with Xavier/Normal initialization
try t.fillRandomNormal(0.0, 0.02);

// 2D matrix multiply: self = A × B
try result.matmul(&A, &B);

// Spectral norm via power iteration
const sigma = try t.spectralNorm(allocator, 20, 1e-12);

// Binary serialization
try t.save(writer);
var loaded = try Tensor.load(allocator, reader);
```

**Supported operations:**

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| `zeros` / `ones` / `eye` | Standard initializers |
| `fillRandomNormal(mean, std)` | Box-Muller normal sampling |
| `fillRademacher()` | ±1 Rademacher random variables |
| `matmul(A, B)` | Naive O(mnk) matrix multiply |
| `outerProduct(other)` | Outer product → rank-1 matrix |
| `normL2()` | L2 norm (f64 accumulator) |
| `spectralNorm(iters, eps)` | Power iteration largest singular value |
| `mulScalar(s)` / `add` / `sub` | Elementwise arithmetic |
| `save(writer)` / `load(reader)` | Little-endian binary I/O |
| `clone(allocator)` | Deep copy |

**Precision flags:**

```zig
pub const Precision = enum { fp4, fp8, fp16, fp32, fp64 };
pub const TensorFlags = struct {
    in_tensor_memory: bool = false,  // Placed in B200 TMEM
    requires_grad:    bool = true,
    is_compressed:    bool = false,   // FP4 compressed
};
```

**Allocator interop:**

```zig
var t = try Tensor.initWithArena(&arena, &[_]usize{ 512, 512 });
var t = try Tensor.initWithPool(&pool, dims);
var t = try Tensor.initWithBuddy(&buddy, dims);
```

